# `for (; i < bound; i++) if ($hasContiguousIndex(array, 0)) last = $getOwnContiguousIndex(array, 1);`
# The library's own read of an element tests nothing by itself: its text says that the position lies inside, and it says so behind a test.
# Array and position stand in front of the loop and nothing in the turns writes, so the read was lifted in front of the head, over the test that it stands behind:
# of a list without elements it read what lies behind the storage, in every build; in a hardened build, where the read holds its position against the length, a right program was stopped.
# The three rows say `relies = InBounds` now, as the reads of elements that the walk makes do: what relies on a position lying inside leaves no loop.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: = GetOwnContiguousIndex
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
